{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/408950-can-demons-regonise-each-other","id":408950,"title":"Can demons regonise each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-17T07:49:53-08:00","id":408950,"title":"Can demons regonise each other?","content":"I realise the answer to this question might be hidden somewhere in the rulebook, but I am short on time so if anyone knows the answer to this question I would be very happy.<br /> <br /> To elaborate, my question is really if and how Demons are able to regonise each other between Covers. If I understood it correctly, Aether sense can give you a feeling of an individual being a Demon (or Angel?) in your vicinity, but can it provide more information than that?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the only way to know that a Demon is the same between two Covers would be to observe the switch as it happens. Even then, you couldn't be sure in the future, as Covers can be traded (or is it only contracts that have not yet been put into a Cover that can be traded?). Perhaps the only way to identify yourself is to take your true demonic form? And then even that is not consistent through time...<br /> <br /> So, well, any insights? What did I miss in the rules?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Damnit, I can't edit my obviousy misspelt topic. It's supposed to be recognise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","user":"Lorsa","date":". 02-17-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:15:08-08:00","id":409034,"title":"","content":"No, there isn't, short of using some kind of power to mark Unchained you've met. As well it should be - hard to be the penultimate liar and a spy game if you're easy to recognize on sight. Most demons develop code names for this very reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:18:58-08:00","id":409041,"title":"","content":"No, you're pretty much right on the money. One of Demon's big themes is that it's nearly impossible to really be sure who someone is. If someone you've never met before comes up to you and acts like they're one of the demons from your ring, it can be very hard to tell whether its actually them in a new Cover or someone else completely pretending to be them. Heck, it might not even be an Unchained; it could be a human, stigmatic, angel, or some other supernatural. As you said, basically the only way to be sure is to see their demonic form, or perhaps a permanent glitch that they have. There's a <i>reason</i> that demons are so paranoid, even about their close associates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T10:00:25-08:00","id":409065,"title":"","content":"Considering how paranoid my players are usually, this is going to be very, very interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to know I didn't miss anything in the books then.<br /> <br /> Speaking of code names; it appears to me that you need one code name per person you want to be able to reliably identify yourself with. I can see why the Eidetic Memory merit is something all Demons have. Otherwise the game would be unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}